WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.140
- You're going to learn

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:04.260
the top 10 classy communication habits,

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:07.020
and no, I don't normally dress like this,

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.661
and I also make no claims
to be classy myself,

00:00:10.661 --> 00:00:13.170
but what I have done is make a mental list

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.660
of the classiest people I've observed

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.490
and how they communicate.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:20.700
So to be clear, the word
classy is not about income.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.410
This list is about qualities

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:26.490
and how classy people act,
how they handle themselves.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:29.700
The bottom line is anybody can be classy.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.450
Number one, classy people
use a moderate volume.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:35.250
They are not loud.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:37.305
They don't draw attention to themselves

00:00:37.305 --> 00:00:41.130
by being boisterous or
putting on a big show.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:43.560
I'm thinking of a classy
woman I know pretty well.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.390
She teaches college.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:46.680
She's self-controlled.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.540
She uses her inside voice,

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.730
as we call it, not her outside voice,

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:54.570
and at the same time, she's
not timid, shy or soft spoken.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:57.510
She never makes you strain to hear her.

00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:02.160
She uses a moderate, clear,
composed, and confident volume.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.700
Number two, classy people
have a tailored appearance.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:09.480
Appearance is part of
your visual communication.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.760
Classy people look put together rather

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.470
than disheveled or shaggy.

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:14.310
They're clean.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:17.040
They have a recent haircut or styling.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.670
They don't wear
unnecessarily fancy, flashy,

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.280
or trendy name-brand clothing

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.760
or make a big deal out of
showing off their labels.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.680
That's because classy is not

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:31.560
about drawing attention to yourself,

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:34.770
but their clothes tend to
be newish and fit them well.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:37.140
They may have a local tailor, for example,

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:40.170
who alters their clothing
so it fits them right.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:43.650
I'm thinking of a classy guy
I know, he's a physician.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:47.100
He always dresses appropriately
to fit the situation.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:50.490
His clothes tend to look
new rather than worn out.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:53.142
There may also be a
level of sophistication

00:01:53.142 --> 00:01:55.260
to a classy person's taste

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.900
that aren't immediately noticeable,

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:00.119
like the fact that their
clothing is made out

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:04.680
of high quality materials rather
than wearing fast fashion.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.890
Their outfit is coordinated
rather than mismatched.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.450
If they're wearing jewelry,

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:13.980
it tends to be more subtle
rather than eye-catching or loud.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.200
Classy, people tend to have good manners,

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.240
etiquette, and respect for others.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.040
They say, "Please," and, "Thank you."

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:21.510
They greet people well.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:23.520
They have a good understanding of manners,

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.522
especially around eating meals

00:02:25.522 --> 00:02:28.560
and occasions like socializing at parties

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.110
or introducing people to each other,

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:34.680
or how to navigate
differences in social status.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:35.640
If they are out to dinner,

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.480
they interact respectfully
with servers and wait staff.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:40.770
It feels as if this respect

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:43.500
for others is driven by self-respect.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.180
They treat people well not

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:48.428
because the other person has
always somehow earned respect

00:02:48.428 --> 00:02:50.460
in all those situations,

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.250
but because that's the kind
of person that they are.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:56.970
The way they treat others
shows their own good character.

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.400
Number four, classy people
make good eye contact,

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.610
meaning they don't
stare or glare at people

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:05.220
or give them stink eye, for example.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:07.530
They don't use eye
contact to dominate others

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:09.450
or make them feel uncomfortable.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:11.850
They also don't avoid eye contact

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:14.340
or look around the room nervously.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:17.610
They make easy, comfortable eye contact.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:19.680
They look people in the eye long enough

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:23.130
to acknowledge others and
make a brief connection.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:26.280
Number five, classy people remember names.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.590
I ran into a fairly high-status person

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:32.250
I'm around occasionally who
carries herself with class.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:35.640
She uses my name about
once per conversation.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:38.580
I get the feeling that she's
doing it as a good habit,

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:41.580
but also as a sign of respect for me.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.700
She wants me to know that she knows me,

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.340
but people like this
don't overuse your name,

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:50.484
like a pushy salesperson who
says your name every sentence

00:03:50.484 --> 00:03:53.130
as a way to control the conversation

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:55.500
or pretend that they're your best friend.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.210
It's much more straightforward

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.350
for classy people.

00:03:58.350 --> 00:03:59.183
They remember

00:03:59.183 --> 00:04:02.460
and use your name to
communicate that you matter.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:05.340
Number six, classy people
take an interest in others

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:06.990
and listen carefully.

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:08.610
They are not self-centered.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:11.040
They take a genuine
interest in other people,

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:13.190
and they'll spend about
as much time listening

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:15.000
as they do talking.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.300
I know a pretty classy
attorney, a good attorney.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:21.201
He has an interesting life,
but he always asks me a lot

00:04:21.201 --> 00:04:23.310
of questions about how I'm doing.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:26.310
He doesn't talk much about
himself unless you ask.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:28.530
Classy people ask you some questions

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.210
about yourself to either catch up

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:32.130
with you and how you've been doing

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:34.530
or as an attempt to
get to know you better,

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:35.640
what you do for a living,

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.950
and learn a bit about your background

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:40.620
as they listen carefully when you speak.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:44.010
Number seven, classy people
pause before speaking.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.330
They aren't in a rush.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:46.950
There's no hurry.

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:49.110
So you'll notice that
when other people speak,

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:50.370
classy people listen

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:54.330
and even pause noticeably
before talking next.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:56.160
I know a successful business owner

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.589
and his wife who also owns
her own successful business,

00:04:59.589 --> 00:05:02.852
and I'm always amazed at
how consistently they pause

00:05:02.852 --> 00:05:06.300
to make sure I've
finished my talking turn.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:09.600
They're pausing to process
what I was just saying,

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:11.730
and they take their time to patiently

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:13.110
form their own thoughts.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:15.774
That's why classy people
will rarely cut others off

00:05:15.774 --> 00:05:18.060
in a conversation or interrupt.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.260
That little pause leads

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.780
to lots of good communication outcomes,

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:24.060
and it comes across as really classy.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:24.893
Number eight,

00:05:24.893 --> 00:05:27.390
classy people have a
generally positive attitude.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.340
You'll seldom hear them complain,

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:30.930
at least not for very long.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.610
They're not all doom and gloom.

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:34.020
Instead, they'll spend their time

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.910
making complimentary remarks

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:39.900
and focusing on the positive
aspects of the situation.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:42.930
They tend to be agreeable and cooperative

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:46.740
in conversations rather than
conflictual or argumentative.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:47.573
They may have a point

00:05:47.573 --> 00:05:50.370
of view, and if there is a
problem, they'll talk about it,

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.650
but they'll also talk about solutions.

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:54.660
They're ultimately looking for the good

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:57.060
in a situation and they focus on that.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:59.400
Number nine, classy people
are not long-winded,

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.920
and they don't dominate conversations.

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.830
I've rarely seen a classy
person who I would describe

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:09.060
as a motor mouth, but I know
lots of people who talk a lot.

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:10.740
I talk for a living.

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:12.682
Still, classy people are usually concise

00:06:12.682 --> 00:06:15.990
and make an effort to
share the talk time equally

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:18.120
with other people in conversations.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:20.089
They tend not to dominate and talk so much

00:06:20.089 --> 00:06:22.830
that others don't get
a chance to contribute.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.870
And this goes well beyond listening

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:26.544
that I mentioned a moment ago.

00:06:26.544 --> 00:06:28.590
For example, in a group situation,

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:30.210
I've often seen classy people look

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:33.240
for ways to involve less talkative people,

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.490
perhaps by asking them a
question to invite them

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.740
into the group conversation.

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:40.227
Number 10, they know when not to speak.

00:06:40.227 --> 00:06:44.490
This behavior is so subtle
that it's easy to miss.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.020
They think before they speak

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:48.990
so they don't say
something they'll regret.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:51.600
In many cases, they won't say anything.

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:54.960
It almost comes across like
wisdom when you see it.

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:56.024
Classy people can sense

00:06:56.024 --> 00:06:58.860
when a conversation is turning into gossip

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:02.185
or negativity, or heading in
a direction that's unhelpful,

00:07:02.185 --> 00:07:04.170
and they know how to stay out of it

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:05.730
and how not to say anything

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:08.370
that would encourage more negativity.

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:09.710
They might just smile and nod

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:11.760
and wait for the moment to pass,

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:14.713
but I've seen them gracefully
exit a group conversation

00:07:14.713 --> 00:07:16.260
if the tide turns

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:19.290
to a topic they don't want
to be associated with.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:21.990
These are the top 10 classy behaviors.

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:23.128
What else would you add

00:07:23.128 --> 00:07:25.710
to the list if you
could suggest something,

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:28.650
and what behaviors would you
personally like to improve upon

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:29.760
that we've been talking about?

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:32.640
Feel free to leave a
comment about that below.

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:35.493
Until next time, thanks,
God bless, and stay classy.

